(3239292, 448820, 21816, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by asif:</b></div><hr/><i> it certainly deserves a ribbon. but what i don''t get is who''s won it. it was your wife''s idea and she pressed the button too. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Valid question. The rules do state that someone else may press the shutter for you as long as you have set up the shot. The reason my wife pressed the shutter was that it was a lot easier for her to do it than me, as I was under water. And yes, she came up with the idea...can''t argue with that!</td>', 'Originally posted by asif: it certainly deserves a ribbon. but what i don''t get is who''s won it. it was your wife''s idea and she pressed the button too.   Valid question. The rules do state that someone else may press the shutter for you as long as you have set up the shot. The reason my wife pressed the shutter was that it was a lot easier for her to do it than me, as I was under water. And yes, she came up with the idea...can''t argue with that!', '2007-01-16 08:38:36.000000', NULL, 0),
